description:
Who are we?
SupportYourApp is a global Intelligent Support-as-a-Service leader, partnering with tech companies and industry leaders like MasterCard, Calm and MacPaw in 30+ countries since 2010 to deliver secure customer and technical support. We operate globally, supporting clients in 60 languages across diverse industries. So what if you had a chance to be a part of the world’s leading SaaS, software, or hardware solutions?
Join our community as a L2 Technical Support Consultant today and thrive in a multicultural and multilingual environment while enjoying your home office. Unlock your potential by mastering new skills and achieving challenging goals in cooperation with our People First management approach. Excited? Let’s see what it takes.
What you will do:

• Deliver outstanding technical support via emails, phone calls and chats;

• Take ownership of technical issues reported by customers and triage them as needed;

• Analyze and resolve customer inquiries containing technical issues or feedback;

• Follow procedures for proper escalation to relevant internal teams and key stakeholders;

• Maintain accurate records of failures, maintenance activities, and bugs;

• Contribute to and maintain the company’s support knowledge base and related documentation;

• Ensure compliance with the company’s Service Level Agreements (SLAs);

What you need to succeed in this role:

•
Excellent English communication skills (C1 for both spoken and written) ;

• At least 1-2 years of proven experience in a Technical Support Engineer, Systems Administrator , or Advanced Support Specialist role;

• Hands-on experience with Windows and Linux operating systems , with a strict emphasis on command-line interface (CLI) and terminal-based management;

• Hands-on experience in diagnosing, troubleshooting, and resolving hardware-related issues in technical environments;

• Solid understanding of hardware and software interactions , including how system components work together to ensure functionality and performance;

• Experience navigating and analyzing system logs , extracting relevant information, and interpreting data to identify and diagnose technical issues;

• Strong troubleshooting and analytical skills, with the ability to investigate complex technical issues, adapt to changing situations, and identify effective solutions;

• Customer-oriented and responsible attitude;

• Personal computer (at least 8Gb of RAM) with a stable internet connection (minimum 50 Mbps-download and 40 Mbps-upload);

Will be a great plus:

• Experience with UAV/UAS systems, flight controllers, or embedded hardware;

• Hands-on experience with network-related architecture and cloud-based systems;

• Experience with and understanding of firewalls and port configuration;

• Experience with remote hardware debugging and low-level system diagnostic tools.

Benefits:

• Flexible schedule;

• Opportunity to cooperate fully remotely ;

• Inclusive international environment;

• Compensation in USD;

• Rewards for referring friends;

• Balance between project workload and personal time, but also - internal health policy;

• Responsive leadership interested in your development and long-lasting cooperation;

• Greenhouse conditions for self-development;

• A culture built on trust, with no time-tracking requirements;

*The items listed in this section may vary depending on the terms of your engagement. Certain benefits and conditions typically apply to employees; independent contractors may not be eligible for all of these. The specific terms, including compensation, benefits, and work conditions, will be clearly defined in your agreement if selected.
You can learn more about the company and its culture by visiting our official website and social pages on Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn.
So if you're a proactive Support Specialist who thrives on solving problems, ensuring customer satisfaction, and delivering outstanding service, don't miss this opportunity and send us your CV

Volunteer Program at PE Insights

Nordic's Largest PE Conference. Stockholm, November 24th &amp; 25th 2027

&nbsp;

Ready to take a major leap towards private equity, M&amp;A, banking or consulting? This is your chance to get a view behind the scenes of the world’s largest private equity community and be part of the volunteer team shaping the future of finance.

Challenge yourself to go outside your comfort zone with likeminded individuals who for two days will be your partners in the trenches facilitating the room of top-of-the pyramid PE professionals.

&nbsp;

Why Private Equity Insights

Private Equity Insights is the world’s largest Private Equity community with 1m PE professionals, delivering impact through 12 global PE conferences with thousands of the most world’s best investors and operators such as Blackstone, BlackRock, Apollo, Carlyle, CVC, KKR, and many more.&nbsp;

Private Equity Insights is part of United Media (https://www.united-media.com/) which focuses on building large-scale industry media and conferences products in sectors such as insurance, finance, retail, etc. As of today, we have organically launched 5 media companies and exited 1.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What we offer you

You’ll be supporting the Private Equity Insights team in delivering the conference for sharp insights and inspiration, and outstanding network opportunities for the PE professionals we serve. Among other things the opportunity offer:

• Peer network: you join a select group of ambitious volunteers who will keep crossing your path for the next 40 years working in the industry.

• Insider knowledge. Where the day allows, you can sit in on panels, the same ones attendees come to hear. In fact, we encourage you to do so.

• Confidence under pressure: after two demanding conference days, high-stakes moments at work will feel easier.

• Master persuasion: learn to influence high-caliber professionals to deliver win-win results.&nbsp;

• A certificate to show on your CV and LinkedIn that you volunteered at Private Equity Insights.&nbsp;

• Fuel: food and refreshments on both days.

• Global programme: The long term opportunity to lead teams and become the person who shows the way for others, or even join Private Equity Insights full time.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Your responsibilities

This is hands-on, operational work focusing on making the conference run. The work changes hour by hour, and you are expected to step in and help wherever the conference needs you.

&nbsp;

What the future hold for you with PE Insights&nbsp;

Whether you are with us for 1 conference or 10+, we believe this lays the foundation for a very successful career.&nbsp;

Exceptional volunteers have in the past been offered roles at Private Equity Insights, such as Investor Relations or Entrepreneur in Residence.

Others have gone on to join firms such as McKinsey, BCG, JP Morgan, Deutsche Bank, Ardian and Verdane.

&nbsp;

What we expect from you

We are looking for final-year undergraduates, master's students and early-career professionals with an interest in private equity, M&amp;A, banking, consulting or conferences. We expect you to:

• Have a relentless drive to become the very best at what you do

• Bring outstanding energy and a positive mindset from the first hour to the last

• Set aside 2 full days for the conference + online training leading up to

• Be curious to learn from top private equity professionals

• Stand out as the person others want beside them on a hard day

• Speak English at a professional level. Spanish is a plus

&nbsp;

This is an unpaid role. Applicants from outside Stockholm are welcome. You fully arrange your own travel and accommodation.&nbsp;

We review every application and invite shortlisted candidates to a short call. If you hold yourself to the standard described here, apply.
